1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Norn

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
It's the same hell I did

3
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
I have to help her whatever it takes

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It doesn't matter if she hates me and Aisha

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
It doesn't matter if she hates it here and doesn't wanna live with us

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
She's my little sister

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Excuse me

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
It's a big brother's job to protect his siblings

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
To never turn his back on them

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Someone is going to pay

11
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:44,910
Oh, um, Mr. Grayrat, I'm sorry we're in the middle of class right now.

12
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:47,470
I won't take long. You have a few minutes, don't you?

13
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:49,010
But...

14
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:54,450
As I suspect you may have already noticed, one of your classmates has stopped showing up.

15
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:58,930
But what you may not know, that girl is my little sister, Norn.

16
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:02,830
I haven't been able to speak with her yet, so I don't have all the details.

17
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:07,130
But there are only so many reasons that a kid her age would stop coming to class.

18
00:03:07,670 --> 00:03:11,590
I believe someone in this room is responsible for one of them.

19
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:15,370
Who was it? Who's bullying her?

20
00:03:17,090 --> 00:03:21,430
Was it you? Or you? Or you?

21
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:26,530
Those involved, please step up. I'm not going to yell at you.

22
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:31,710
I just want you to understand that my sister was hurt and apologized to her.

23
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:34,450
And after that, I'll tear you limb from limb.

24
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:37,410
I don't care if they're the actual bullies or not.

25
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:39,990
Anyone who turned a blind eye is just as guilty.

26
00:03:41,410 --> 00:03:42,550
Now fess up!

27
00:03:46,670 --> 00:03:47,910
Oh, um...

28
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:50,470
Pardon me.

29
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:51,610
Yes?

30
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:55,310
Um, okay. Well, I, um...

31
00:03:55,310 --> 00:03:57,530
I was actually talking to Norn the other day.

32
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:00,910
I see. You said something hurtful by accident, right?

33
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:02,830
No, nothing like that.

34
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:06,650
It's just, I've heard a lot of stories about you, Mr. Great Rat.

35
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:09,350
But Norn is more of an ordinary girl.

36
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:12,990
I just pointed out that you're pretty different from each other.

37
00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:14,710
And she got really angry.

38
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:15,490
What?

39
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:17,250
That doesn't make any sense.

40
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:19,290
Norn doesn't want to be like me.

41
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:21,130
So why...

42
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:21,810
Oh...

43
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:23,590
Did something come to mind, ma'am?

44
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,010
Yes. One thing.

45
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:29,070
I was returning a homework assignment that she had done a bit poorly on.

46
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:30,510
And so is punishment.

47
00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:33,070
You stripped her naked in the faculty office. Is that it?

48
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:34,370
No. Heavens.

49
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:37,170
I simply said to try harder next time.

50
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:40,470
That if she followed her big brother's example, she'd be doing well.

51
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:41,010
And...

52
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:45,810
She said she'd try, but she looked about ready to burst into tears.

53
00:04:46,030 --> 00:04:46,570
Poor thing.

54
00:04:47,710 --> 00:04:48,110
Wait.

55
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:53,550
Yeah, now that you mention it.

56
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:55,010
I may have said...

57
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:55,690
Me too.

58
00:04:55,690 --> 00:05:11,430
It was my fault.

59
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,110
No wonder she couldn't stand it.

60
00:05:14,970 --> 00:05:16,630
People have always compared her to Aisha.

61
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:19,270
Now they're doing it with a brother she hates.

62
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:21,990
Damn it.

63
00:05:25,690 --> 00:05:26,890
I heard what happened.

64
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:29,250
Don't blame yourself, Rudy.

65
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:31,050
Too late for that.

66
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:33,570
But I guess I'll try.

67
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:36,490
Yeah, Meow. None of that is your fault, boss man.

68
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:37,310
Yeah, for sure.

69
00:05:37,590 --> 00:05:38,770
You didn't do anything.

70
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:40,610
I appreciate it.

71
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,750
And thank you for letting me know about Norn.

72
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:45,550
Sorry I dragged you over to her classroom.

73
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:47,310
That was dumb.

74
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:48,650
And embarrassing.

75
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:52,390
There's nothing dumb about sticking up for your family, Meow.

76
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:54,530
I've got a little sister, too.

77
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:56,450
So I know how that stuff can be.

78
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,050
Meow, what a tough performance.

79
00:05:58,450 --> 00:05:59,410
You got scary.

80
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:05,670
So, Meow what?

81
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:07,390
Are you gonna try to talk to her?

82
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:09,010
We could send a message for you.

83
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:11,110
I don't think that would do any good.

84
00:06:11,890 --> 00:06:13,550
She hold herself up because of me.

85
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:15,150
Because of me.

86
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:17,790
She's a shut-in because of me.

87
00:06:18,270 --> 00:06:20,730
Well, Lina and I could always drag her to class.

88
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:21,630
Yeah, easy.

89
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:24,090
If she stays in there too long, her brain will be goop.

90
00:06:24,210 --> 00:06:25,510
Yup, you got that right.

91
00:06:25,590 --> 00:06:27,110
Then she'll be as stupid as Lina.

92
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:29,190
Persina's right on the money, boss.

93
00:06:30,170 --> 00:06:30,570
Meow.

94
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,490
What's that supposed to mean?

95
00:06:32,510 --> 00:06:33,650
That her brain is goop.

96
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:36,350
People don't stop going outside because it's fun.

97
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:38,830
She's got a reason.

98
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:41,590
And us dragging her out won't change that.

99
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:45,650
Matter of fact, it's way more likely that'll just make the whole thing worse.

100
00:06:46,410 --> 00:06:48,470
But, I don't know.

101
00:06:48,570 --> 00:06:49,710
I can't just ignore this.

102
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:52,630
If she stays in there too long, I know I...

103
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:54,050
She'll regret it.

104
00:06:56,130 --> 00:06:56,530
Rudy.

105
00:06:56,530 --> 00:07:01,790
Hey, Rudy.

106
00:07:07,910 --> 00:07:08,390
Think.

107
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:10,310
I have to do something.

108
00:07:14,050 --> 00:07:14,890
But what?

109
00:07:15,490 --> 00:07:16,790
Nothing ever helped me.

110
00:07:19,990 --> 00:07:20,430
Rudy!

111
00:07:20,430 --> 00:07:26,030
I mean, we're serious about helping out with your whole sister thing, you know.

112
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,990
Yeah, you're always looking out for us.

113
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,010
It's only fair.

114
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:30,630
That really is kind of you.

115
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,890
But I still don't...

116
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:34,690
Don't you worry about nothing, boss.

117
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:36,190
I got a great idea already.

118
00:07:36,930 --> 00:07:38,510
The dorms sure cleared up fast.

119
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:39,210
What's the deal?

120
00:07:39,450 --> 00:07:42,070
Princess Ariel's giving a speech in the dining hall.

121
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:43,350
Wait, are you for real?

122
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:44,850
Talk about impromptu.

123
00:07:44,850 --> 00:07:47,870
Well, come on, or she's gonna start without us.

124
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:50,590
Rudy.

125
00:07:52,150 --> 00:07:53,450
Well, we're a go.

126
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,350
The dorm is practically empty now.

127
00:07:56,230 --> 00:07:57,390
Exactly as planned.

128
00:07:57,990 --> 00:07:59,690
Ariel's speeches always draw a crowd.

129
00:08:00,290 --> 00:08:00,590
Okay.

130
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:03,450
I'll sneak into the girl's wing and see if I can reach Norn.

131
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:04,850
Good.

132
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:06,910
Please give Princess Ariel my thanks.

133
00:08:07,850 --> 00:08:08,710
And the other two?

134
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:10,030
In position.

135
00:08:10,550 --> 00:08:12,890
And hey, I'm sorry I couldn't be more help.

136
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:13,930
What?

137
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:17,310
Well, I stopped by Norn's room earlier today to check up on her.

138
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:19,370
But she didn't want to see me either.

139
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:22,890
It's more than enough that you even tried.

140
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:24,030
Don't worry.

141
00:08:24,770 --> 00:08:26,290
I'll work it out with Norn somehow.

142
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:42,510
Thanks for the inn.

143
00:08:42,510 --> 00:08:43,890
You ready to roll?

144
00:08:51,270 --> 00:08:53,510
Just watch where you're going next time.

145
00:08:53,790 --> 00:08:54,150
Yeah.

146
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:54,750
I know.

147
00:08:54,810 --> 00:08:55,310
I'm sorry.

148
00:09:01,210 --> 00:09:01,570
Norn.

149
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:03,370
Hang in there.

150
00:09:03,550 --> 00:09:04,070
I'm coming.

151
00:09:05,450 --> 00:09:06,270
Made it, Meow.

152
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:11,270
Your sister's room is at the end of the hall on the right.

153
00:09:11,270 --> 00:09:25,790
Norn, it's me, Rudeus.

154
00:09:26,130 --> 00:09:27,030
Can I come in?

155
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:32,390
You awake?

156
00:09:32,390 --> 00:09:38,490
Stay out.

157
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:38,510
Stay out.

158
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:39,450
Let me see.

159
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:49,450
No, you.

160
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:56,450
Now we're going to be...

161
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:01,170
After the inn I'll be...

162
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:15,370
Norton.

163
00:10:15,370 --> 00:10:34,670
When I first became a shut-in, my older brother came to visit me like this.

164
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:38,770
He hit me with all kinds of common sense and reasonably sound arguments.

165
00:10:38,770 --> 00:10:43,630
There are people out there who have it worse than you.

166
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:47,210
If you run away from all your problems, you'll be running forever.

167
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:52,070
It may hurt now, but the regret will hurt worse.

168
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:53,070
Then the bargaining.

169
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:55,570
You don't have to go back to school right away.

170
00:10:55,570 --> 00:10:56,570
That can wait.

171
00:10:56,570 --> 00:10:59,750
At least come out and have lunch with me.

172
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:02,830
I spit on all of it.

173
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:06,510
Didn't try to argue, didn't look at him, just ignored him.

174
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:10,430
Stayed totally silent till he was gone.

175
00:11:10,430 --> 00:11:27,810
I convinced myself that someone like him couldn't possibly know how I felt.

176
00:11:27,810 --> 00:11:32,570
I think now I know how he felt to some extent.

177
00:11:32,570 --> 00:11:36,250
He was there for a long time, but eventually he left.

178
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:39,310
It's not hard to imagine why.

179
00:11:39,310 --> 00:11:44,390
So I worry that if I back off now, Norn may stay in this room forever.

180
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:45,390
I can't just turn and run.

181
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:46,390
I won't.

182
00:11:46,390 --> 00:11:47,390
I won't.

183
00:11:47,390 --> 00:11:51,390
Not this time.

184
00:11:51,390 --> 00:11:55,730
you're doing your point.

185
00:11:55,730 --> 00:12:00,050
I can only be réponse.

186
00:12:00,050 --> 00:12:00,650
Brother.

187
00:12:00,650 --> 00:12:05,590
I wonder...

188
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:19,150
I wonder, when exactly did I start to be afraid of him?

189
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:24,230
The first time we met, he punched my dad in the face.

190
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:27,310
The dad who'd kept me safe all that time.

191
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:29,430
Who always put me first.

192
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:31,730
Who loved me more than anything.

193
00:12:33,230 --> 00:12:34,230
Stop it!

194
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:37,150
Leave him alone!

195
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:41,810
I wasn't about to accept a monster like that as part of my family.

196
00:12:43,310 --> 00:12:45,210
I wasn't scared of him then.

197
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:47,130
I just hated him.

198
00:12:48,270 --> 00:12:54,050
And when I finally saw him again, he'd been out getting drunk with some woman hanging all over him.

199
00:12:55,070 --> 00:12:58,190
My dad is out there looking everywhere for my mom.

200
00:12:58,830 --> 00:13:00,310
He could be someplace dangerous.

201
00:13:00,310 --> 00:13:04,630
And there he was, looking like he couldn't be happier.

202
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:07,610
No one here cares about us.

203
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:10,630
So I just have to make sure I don't upset them.

204
00:13:12,490 --> 00:13:14,530
I don't want them to kick me out.

205
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:16,850
It's too cold.

206
00:13:17,290 --> 00:13:18,350
I won't make it.

207
00:13:18,350 --> 00:13:23,570
Okay then.

208
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:25,410
I'll try living in the dorm.

209
00:13:29,910 --> 00:13:32,110
Not what I expected, but...

210
00:13:32,110 --> 00:13:33,170
Don't let her!

211
00:13:33,410 --> 00:13:36,210
Dad told us we had to come here and live with our big brother!

212
00:13:36,210 --> 00:13:41,230
If you're sure, then yeah.

213
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:42,950
I think we can arrange that.

214
00:13:43,470 --> 00:13:44,510
That's not fair!

215
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:47,110
Why isn't he getting angry?

216
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:49,770
I thought he'd yell at me for being selfish.

217
00:13:50,650 --> 00:13:53,130
Maybe he's just not interested in me at all.

218
00:13:53,130 --> 00:13:56,470
Yeah, I bet I'm in his way.

219
00:13:58,150 --> 00:14:02,090
For some reason, that makes me feel a little sad.

220
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:05,910
It's a pleasure to meet all of you.

221
00:14:06,510 --> 00:14:07,930
My name is Norn Greyrat.

222
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:09,450
Greyrat?

223
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:11,450
Like those Greyrats?

224
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:16,650
Hey Norn, are you related to Rudeus Greyrat by chance?

225
00:14:16,650 --> 00:14:18,930
I am.

226
00:14:19,610 --> 00:14:20,890
The Rudeus?

227
00:14:21,150 --> 00:14:22,870
He's the strongest guy in the school.

228
00:14:22,890 --> 00:14:24,010
That is so cool!

229
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:28,210
Sister, huh?

230
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:29,910
What was it like growing up with him?

231
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:31,530
Like, does he teach you magic and stuff?

232
00:14:31,590 --> 00:14:32,670
Oh, I bet so.

233
00:14:32,770 --> 00:14:35,030
You must be some kind of magical genius yourself.

234
00:14:35,290 --> 00:14:36,550
Your brother is incredible.

235
00:14:37,010 --> 00:14:37,950
I mean, he's so talented.

236
00:14:37,970 --> 00:14:38,790
You're so lucky.

237
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:41,210
I wish I had a brother even half as cool as you do.

238
00:14:42,210 --> 00:14:43,650
Your name is...

239
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:46,150
Norn Greyrat.

240
00:14:46,150 --> 00:14:48,630
Excuse me.

241
00:14:49,470 --> 00:14:51,910
Hey, you're Rudeus' little sister, aren't you?

242
00:14:53,230 --> 00:14:54,030
I am.

243
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:55,230
My name is Norn.

244
00:14:55,350 --> 00:14:55,930
Oh, perfect.

245
00:14:56,010 --> 00:14:57,510
We've been looking all over for you

246
00:14:57,510 --> 00:14:59,770
because he helped us learn some magic a little while back.

247
00:15:00,090 --> 00:15:01,490
Would you tell him we said thanks again?

248
00:15:03,130 --> 00:15:04,370
I'm sorry, ma'am.

249
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:05,770
That's all right.

250
00:15:05,850 --> 00:15:06,870
It's your first assignment.

251
00:15:07,310 --> 00:15:08,190
You just got here.

252
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:12,410
I'm sure you'll follow in your brother's footsteps soon enough.

253
00:15:13,110 --> 00:15:14,330
No, I won't.

254
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:14,370
I won't.

255
00:15:16,150 --> 00:15:18,490
Hey.

256
00:15:19,030 --> 00:15:19,530
Yes?

257
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:21,550
Tell me something about your brother.

258
00:15:22,310 --> 00:15:23,830
I don't want to.

259
00:15:23,830 --> 00:15:33,810
Are you curious about your brother hanging around with Princess Ariel?

260
00:15:34,230 --> 00:15:35,750
You needn't worry about it.

261
00:15:36,030 --> 00:15:37,890
Despite appearances, your brother is...

262
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:38,990
I don't care.

263
00:15:38,990 --> 00:15:48,870
You needn't worry about your brother hanging around with Princess Ariel.

264
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:49,370
Seriously?

265
00:15:49,370 --> 00:15:50,250
What were you thinking?

266
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:52,430
I got in trouble with the Princess for that.

267
00:15:52,650 --> 00:15:53,610
Ah, look.

268
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:54,590
It's Rudeus.

269
00:15:54,730 --> 00:15:56,370
Did I tell you I talked to him one time?

270
00:15:56,590 --> 00:15:57,030
What?

271
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,270
Ah, lucky.

272
00:15:58,270 --> 00:16:01,850
Why does everyone get like this about him?

273
00:16:01,850 --> 00:16:01,870
Why does everyone get like this about him?

274
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:01,890
Why does everyone get like this about him?

275
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:02,690
No, I can't.

276
00:16:02,730 --> 00:16:03,210
No, I can't.

277
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:21,130
What?

278
00:16:21,130 --> 00:16:40,010
I just don't understand him.

279
00:16:41,070 --> 00:16:42,230
Because I worry.

280
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,350
Hey, cut him some slack.

281
00:16:47,430 --> 00:16:49,070
I don't want to. I hate him.

282
00:16:49,610 --> 00:16:50,750
Well, don't do that.

283
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:52,170
Rudy's had it rough.

284
00:16:53,210 --> 00:16:55,430
Dad said stuff like that all the time.

285
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:58,490
I guess I was too little to understand what he meant.

286
00:16:59,390 --> 00:17:01,550
But now I think I kind of get it.

287
00:17:02,190 --> 00:17:04,830
Maybe he was having a hard time about something.

288
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:07,730
Maybe we're actually more alike than I thought.

289
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:10,930
But what am I supposed to do about it?

290
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:13,790
How do I just talk things out with him now?

291
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:16,190
How did Dad make up with him?

292
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:17,910
I don't know.

293
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:21,250
I don't know and no one here will help me.

294
00:17:23,090 --> 00:17:24,190
I don't know.

295
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:29,450
What's wrong?

296
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:37,550
I want to go back to Eastport and see my dad.

297
00:17:38,170 --> 00:17:40,330
You dislike Rudeus that much, do you?

298
00:17:41,690 --> 00:17:42,510
I do.

299
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:45,270
I can see why.

300
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:48,090
But he's more than your poor first impression of him.

301
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:49,830
He's strong, clever.

302
00:17:50,470 --> 00:17:52,150
A warrior worthy of respect.

303
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:54,950
That doesn't make sense.

304
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:57,630
It will someday when you're older.

305
00:17:58,590 --> 00:18:01,990
The next time you see him, keep your chin up and don't run.

306
00:18:01,990 --> 00:18:05,470
Family bonds can nearly always be mended.

307
00:18:06,110 --> 00:18:08,410
If you don't believe me, just remember this.

308
00:18:08,990 --> 00:18:11,090
Your father didn't run from him, did he?

309
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:24,370
Rudeus.

310
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:27,150
Lorne, I'm sorry.

311
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:30,250
You've had it rough from the minute you got here.

312
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,270
You finally got a fresh start.

313
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:37,310
And it turned out like this because of me.

314
00:18:39,210 --> 00:18:40,790
I don't know what to say.

315
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:46,930
It's like, or it is, I just don't know you.

316
00:18:46,930 --> 00:18:52,410
I realize how hard this must be, but I don't know what I can do to help.

317
00:19:16,930 --> 00:19:25,550
But, I do know, I want to be here for you.

318
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:28,590
I want to understand you.

319
00:19:30,030 --> 00:19:34,370
So, do you mind if I stay?

320
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:41,290
He really is just like my dad.

321
00:19:41,970 --> 00:19:43,650
I can't be scared of that.

322
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:47,010
He was never going to hit me at all, was he?

323
00:19:47,670 --> 00:19:50,190
And I know he won't hit dad anymore either.

324
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:52,630
So, I guess I should.

325
00:19:52,630 --> 00:19:52,670
I should.

326
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:23,250
Hey, and good morning, big brother.

327
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:24,890
Oh, hello.

328
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:26,490
Good morning, Lorne.

329
00:20:26,750 --> 00:20:28,670
And to you as well, Sophie.

330
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:30,490
You look really nice.

331
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:31,230
Thanks.

332
00:20:31,570 --> 00:20:32,950
It's so good to see you, Lorne.

333
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:37,370
Oh, look at her.

334
00:20:37,730 --> 00:20:40,090
She's so much more cheerful since you talked to her.

335
00:20:40,090 --> 00:20:43,170
Not my doing.

336
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,330
I barely said anything at all.

337
00:20:46,190 --> 00:20:49,710
Lorne never told me what she was upset about or what she'd been feeling.

338
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:51,550
And I may never know.

339
00:20:52,410 --> 00:20:54,010
She just cried for a long time.

340
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:56,090
And yet...

341
00:20:56,090 --> 00:20:58,490
Something tells me she's going to be all right.

342
00:20:59,370 --> 00:21:02,070
She must have worked through those tough feelings on her own.

343
00:21:03,290 --> 00:21:03,810
Atta girl.

344
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:08,690
At ten, she pulled off something I was never able to manage in my past life.

345
00:21:09,550 --> 00:21:13,210
If I'd been more like her back then, I wonder.

346
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:14,990
Rudy?

347
00:21:16,730 --> 00:21:18,210
Hey, what's the matter?

348
00:21:18,630 --> 00:21:18,990
Nothing.

349
00:21:19,190 --> 00:21:19,690
Just thinking.

350
00:21:20,190 --> 00:21:21,750
I can't change my past.

351
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:24,470
I can't fix the relationships I broke.

352
00:21:24,470 --> 00:21:27,990
And I'll never know how my family really felt back then.

353
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:34,470
But I still feel like something that was stuck between my teeth for a long time finally broke free.

354
00:21:35,110 --> 00:21:37,270
I take it you'll be all right now, too?

355
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:39,810
Well, we should probably get going.

356
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:43,150
We still need to thank Princess Ariel and get her up to speed.

357
00:21:43,450 --> 00:21:43,730
Yeah.

358
00:21:44,150 --> 00:21:46,150
I need to find Lini and Persina, too.

359
00:21:46,150 --> 00:21:55,570
If Nanahoshi does manage to return to our old world someday, I'll have to ask her to get a message to my brother.

360
00:21:57,610 --> 00:22:00,230
I'm sorry for everything I put you through back then.

361
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:02,650
And thank you.

362
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:40,020
La-ya-la-ya-la

